{
  "quotes": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Stay hungry, stay foolish.",
      "author": "Steve Jobs",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": 2005,
      "source": "Stanford Commencement",
      "tags": ["innovation", "learning"]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Code is like humor. When you have to explain it, it's bad.",
      "author": "Cory House",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Twitter",
      "tags": ["coding", "humor"]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Talk is cheap. Show me the code.",
      "author": "Linus Torvalds",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": 2000,
      "source": "Linux Mailing List",
      "tags": ["action", "programming"]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The only way to learn a new programming language is by writing programs in it.",
      "author": "Dennis Ritchie",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": 1978,
      "source": "The C Programming Language",
      "tags": ["learning", "programming"]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Experience is the name everyone gives to their mistakes.",
      "author": "Oscar Wilde",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": 1892,
      "source": "Lady Windermere's Fan",
      "tags": ["experience", "learning"]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Any fool can write code that a computer can understand. Good programmers write code that humans can understand.",
      "author": "Martin Fowler",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": 2008,
      "source": "Refactoring",
      "tags": ["clean code", "programming"]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "First, solve the problem. Then, write the code.",
      "author": "John Johnson",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Unknown",
      "tags": ["problem-solving", "programming"]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "The best way to predict the future is to invent it.",
      "author": "Alan Kay",
      "category": "innovation",
      "year": 1971,
      "source": "Xerox PARC",
      "tags": ["innovation", "future"]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "Simplicity is the soul of efficiency.",
      "author": "Austin Freeman",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": 1907,
      "source": "The Eye of Osiris",
      "tags": ["simplicity", "efficiency"]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "text": "Make it work, make it right, make it fast.",
      "author": "Kent Beck",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Extreme Programming",
      "tags": ["development", "best practices"]
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "text": "Innovation distinguishes between a leader and a follower.",
      "author": "Steve Jobs",
      "category": "innovation",
      "year": 1998,
      "source": "Think Different Campaign",
      "tags": ["innovation", "leadership"]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "text": "The greatest glory in living lies not in never falling, but in rising every time we fall.",
      "author": "Nelson Mandela",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Speeches",
      "tags": ["resilience", "perseverance"]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "text": "It is during our darkest moments that we must focus to see the light.",
      "author": "Aristotle",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Ancient Philosophy",
      "tags": ["perspective", "resilience"]
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "text": "The only impossible journey is the one you never begin.",
      "author": "Tony Robbins",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Personal Development",
      "tags": ["action", "motivation"]
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "text": "Perfection is not just about control, it is also about letting go.",
      "author": "Steve Jobs",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": 2006,
      "source": "Apple Design Philosophy",
      "tags": ["design", "simplicity"]
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "text": "Life is what happens when you're busy making other plans.",
      "author": "John Lennon",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": 1980,
      "source": "Beautiful Boy",
      "tags": ["life", "perspective"]
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "text": "You miss 100% of the shots you don't take.",
      "author": "Wayne Gretzky",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Sports Philosophy",
      "tags": ["action", "risk-taking"]
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "text": "If you want to go fast, go alone. If you want to go far, go together.",
      "author": "African Proverb",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Traditional Wisdom",
      "tags": ["teamwork", "collaboration"]
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "text": "The only constant in life is change.",
      "author": "Heraclitus",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Ancient Greece",
      "tags": ["change", "adaptation"]
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "text": "It is impossible to live without failing at something.",
      "author": "J.K. Rowling",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": 2008,
      "source": "Harvard Commencement",
      "tags": ["failure", "growth"]
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "text": "The difference between who you are and who you want to be is what you do.",
      "author": "Bill Phillips",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Personal Development",
      "tags": ["action", "self-improvement"]
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "text": "Your time is limited, don't waste it living someone else's life.",
      "author": "Steve Jobs",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": 2005,
      "source": "Stanford Commencement",
      "tags": ["authenticity", "purpose"]
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "text": "The future belongs to those who believe in the beauty of their dreams.",
      "author": "Eleanor Roosevelt",
      "category": "inspiration",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Speeches",
      "tags": ["dreams", "belief"]
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "text": "Don't watch the clock; do what it does. Keep going.",
      "author": "Sam Levenson",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Personal Development",
      "tags": ["persistence", "focus"]
    },
    {
      "id": 25,
      "text": "A journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step.",
      "author": "Lao Tzu",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Tao Te Ching",
      "tags": ["journey", "perseverance"]
    },
    {
      "id": 26,
      "text": "Programs must be written for people to read, and only incidentally for machines to execute.",
      "author": "Harold Abelson",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": 1985,
      "source": "Structure and Interpretation of Computer Programs",
      "tags": ["clean code", "readability"]
    },
    {
      "id": 27,
      "text": "There are two ways to write error-free programs; only the third one works.",
      "author": "Alan Perlis",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Epigrams",
      "tags": ["debugging", "humor"]
    },
    {
      "id": 28,
      "text": "Testing shows the presence, not the absence of bugs.",
      "author": "Edsger Dijkstra",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": 1969,
      "source": "EWD30",
      "tags": ["testing", "quality"]
    },
    {
      "id": 29,
      "text": "Debugging is twice as hard as writing the code in the first place.",
      "author": "Brian Kernighan",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": null,
      "source": "The Practice of Programming",
      "tags": ["debugging", "code quality"]
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "text": "The best performance improvement is the transition from the nonworking state to the working state.",
      "author": "John Ousterhout",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Tcl Programming",
      "tags": ["optimization", "pragmatism"]
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "text": "Don't comment bad code, rewrite it.",
      "author": "Brian Kernighan",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": 1974,
      "source": "The Elements of Programming Style",
      "tags": ["clean code", "refactoring"]
    },
    {
      "id": 32,
      "text": "The most important optimization is simplification.",
      "author": "David Parnas",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Software Engineering",
      "tags": ["optimization", "simplicity"]
    },
    {
      "id": 33,
      "text": "You can't have great software without a great team.",
      "author": "Steve Jobs",
      "category": "innovation",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Business Leadership",
      "tags": ["teamwork", "excellence"]
    },
    {
      "id": 34,
      "text": "Ideas are easy. Implementation is hard.",
      "author": "Evan Williams",
      "category": "innovation",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Startups",
      "tags": ["execution", "action"]
    },
    {
      "id": 35,
      "text": "Success is not final, failure is not fatal.",
      "author": "Winston Churchill",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Speeches",
      "tags": ["perspective", "resilience"]
    },
    {
      "id": 36,
      "text": "The only true wisdom is in knowing you know nothing.",
      "author": "Socrates",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Ancient Philosophy",
      "tags": ["humility", "learning"]
    },
    {
      "id": 37,
      "text": "Be yourself; everyone else is already taken.",
      "author": "Oscar Wilde",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": 1890,
      "source": "Personal Philosophy",
      "tags": ["authenticity", "individuality"]
    },
    {
      "id": 38,
      "text": "Strive for progress, not perfection.",
      "author": "Robin Sharma",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Personal Development",
      "tags": ["progress", "growth"]
    },
    {
      "id": 39,
      "text": "The way to get started is to quit talking and begin doing.",
      "author": "Walt Disney",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Business Philosophy",
      "tags": ["action", "execution"]
    },
    {
      "id": 40,
      "text": "Everything you want is on the other side of fear.",
      "author": "George Addair",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Courage",
      "tags": ["fear", "courage"]
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "text": "Your limitations—real or imagined—do not define your destiny.",
      "author": "Steve Maraboli",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Personal Development",
      "tags": ["potential", "mindset"]
    },
    {
      "id": 42,
      "text": "Do something today that your future self will thank you for.",
      "author": "Sean Patrick Flanery",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Personal Development",
      "tags": ["discipline", "future"]
    },
    {
      "id": 43,
      "text": "Invest in yourself. Your education and self-improvement is the best investment.",
      "author": "Warren Buffett",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Financial Wisdom",
      "tags": ["self-improvement", "learning"]
    },
    {
      "id": 44,
      "text": "The only limit to our realization of tomorrow is our doubts of today.",
      "author": "Franklin D. Roosevelt",
      "category": "motivation",
      "year": 1945,
      "source": "Speeches",
      "tags": ["belief", "determination"]
    },
    {
      "id": 45,
      "text": "Code without tests is bad code. No matter how well it is written.",
      "author": "Robert C. Martin",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": 2008,
      "source": "Clean Code",
      "tags": ["testing", "quality assurance"]
    },
    {
      "id": 46,
      "text": "A good programmer is someone who looks both ways before crossing a one-way street.",
      "author": "Doug Linder",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Programming Humor",
      "tags": ["caution", "humor"]
    },
    {
      "id": 47,
      "text": "Beautiful is better than ugly. Explicit is better than implicit.",
      "author": "Tim Peters",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": 1999,
      "source": "The Zen of Python",
      "tags": ["code philosophy", "clarity"]
    },
    {
      "id": 48,
      "text": "Before software should be reusable, it should be usable.",
      "author": "Ralph Johnson",
      "category": "programming",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Design Patterns",
      "tags": ["pragmatism", "usability"]
    },
    {
      "id": 49,
      "text": "We build our computers the way we build our cities—over time, without a plan.",
      "author": "Ellen Ullman",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Technology Essays",
      "tags": ["complexity", "evolution"]
    },
    {
      "id": 50,
      "text": "The greatest enemy of knowledge is not ignorance, it is the illusion of knowledge.",
      "author": "Daniel J. Boorstin",
      "category": "wisdom",
      "year": null,
      "source": "Philosophy",
      "tags": ["humility", "wisdom"]
    }
